📍 Critical Pins (UART / Power)
RX   TX
118  119
GND  115 or 126


118 → UART1_RX

119 → UART1_TX

GND → Any ground point

115 or 126 → VCCIO (3.3V)

🔌 ESP32 ↔ RK3126C UART Wiring
ESP32	RK3126C	Function
VCC (3.3V)	VCCIO	Power
GND	GND	Ground
TX	UART1_RX	Data
RX	UART1_TX	Receive

⚠️ IMPORTANT

Use 3.3V ONLY

DO NOT apply 5V to RK3126C pins

Always test continuity before powering on

🧠 Technical Notes

UART provides access to boot logs, debug output and possible system interaction

Useful for:

Boot diagnostics

Firmware analysis

ESP32 integration (Wi-Fi / Bluetooth)

Incorrect soldering may permanently brick the device
